1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,569
Why do wheels spin backwards on camera?

2
00:00:02,869 --> 00:00:04,155
The car speeds up.

3
00:00:04,155 --> 00:00:07,657
Its wheels spin backwards, slow down, and freeze.

4
00:00:08,157 --> 00:00:10,751
A camera doesn't film smooth motion.

5
00:00:10,751 --> 00:00:14,138
It takes still pictures, often 30 a second.

6
00:00:14,438 --> 00:00:18,330
Your brain joins them up by picking the shortest move between them.

7
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:22,411
Spin a wheel slowly, and each spoke moves a little.

8
00:00:22,411 --> 00:00:22,933
Forward.

9
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:27,196
Faster, and each spoke lands just short of where the next one was.

10
00:00:27,496 --> 00:00:30,689
The shortest match is now a small step backwards.

11
00:00:30,689 --> 00:00:32,188
So that's what you see.

12
00:00:32,938 --> 00:00:37,166
Land exactly on the next spoke, and the wheel seems to freeze.

13
00:00:37,466 --> 00:00:39,035
The wheel goes forward.

14
00:00:39,035 --> 00:00:40,876
The pictures say backwards.
